# Two data directories, two lifecycles (docs/DATA_CONTRACT.md).
#
#   data/snapshots/   OPERATIONAL. What a collection run writes. May hold
#                     seller-authored prose, so it is never published.
#   data/corpora/     PUBLICATION-GRADE. Written only by
#                     scripts/promote_corpus.py, which redacts and validates.
#                     It is NOT listed here and must not be: D46 is what
#                     happens when the evidence behind a published number is
#                     ignored out of the repository.
data/raw/
data/snapshots/
#   data/inbox/       Messages people sent us through the contact form, with
#                     the contact details they chose to give. Not a corpus,
#                     never published, and deliberately not scanned by the
#                     corpus guards — those exist to keep a SELLER's
#                     identifiers out of a published artifact, which is a
#                     different thing from correspondence addressed to us.
data/inbox/
.DS_Store

